# TASK-260819-16oo3p results

## Outcome

Implemented a fail-closed build-host policy. The current development Mac is registered build-only using a one-way IOPlatformUUID fingerprint; raw identity is not stored or printed. Physical runner preflight/exercise now require explicit opt-in, a non-loopback configured hostname matching the runtime Mac, an available denylist, and a runtime fingerprint distinct from every registered build-only host.

Authoritative policy was added to CONTRIBUTING.md, .spec/validation.md, docs/spawn-policy.md, docs/build-host-safety.md, and the disposable probe runbook. Important findings were recorded in .planning/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_logbook.md.

## Board dependency audit

Directly linked 19 active macOS network-mutating physical validation/release tasks across M1-M5 to human gate TASK-260819-25e1ys. M0 CLI harness-only measurements remain local-safe. Historical accepted P0 task TASK-260715-9yp8to was not reopened; its reusable physical runner is now guarded. task-board validate: exit 0.

## Validation

- bash -n for changed shell scripts: exit 0.
- shellcheck for changed shell scripts: exit 0.
- Probes/macOSPacketTunnelProbe/Scripts/test-physical-gate-p0.sh: exit 0; covers absent opt-in, empty host, localhost aliases, IPv4/IPv6 loopbacks, build-host fingerprint, runtime-host mismatch, positive dedicated-host identity, and guarded preflight/exercise entrypoints.
- Actual build-host check with opt-in plus current hostname: expected exit 1 with build-only prohibition, assertion command exit 0.
- Dependency audit: exit 0, dependency_gate_count=19.
- git diff --check: exit 0.
- make core-test core-build: exit 0; 443 tests passed with 25 recorded known issues for the already unavailable ReluxNIOSSH adapter; Swift build passed.
- Initial documented make test && make app attempt: exit 2 before running anything because those targets did not exist; CONTRIBUTING.md now names make core-test and make core-build.

## Safety evidence

No command installed or opened an application/system extension, accessed real NetworkExtension preferences, called startVPNTunnel, activated a provider, or changed routes/DNS. Negative entrypoint tests fail at the host guard before inspecting their deliberately nonexistent app path. No physical validation was run.
